					<description><![CDATA[<img width="1740" height="2140" src="https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/caprese-gnocchi-recipe.jpg" class="attachment-feed-image size-feed-image wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" srcset="https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/caprese-gnocchi-recipe.jpg 1740w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/caprese-gnocchi-recipe-244x300.jpg 244w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/caprese-gnocchi-recipe-833x1024.jpg 833w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/caprese-gnocchi-recipe-81x100.jpg 81w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/caprese-gnocchi-recipe-580x713.jpg 580w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/caprese-gnocchi-recipe-1160x1427.jpg 1160w" sizes="(max-width: 1740px) 100vw, 1740px" /><br />This Caprese gnocchi recipe is about to become your go-to summer weeknight dinner! It cooks on one pan in under 30 minutes and is bursting with fresh flavor. Inspired by a classic Caprese salad, it combines store-bought gnocchi with summer tomatoes, fresh basil, and creamy mozzarella cheese. Just like in my sheet pan gnocchi recipe, I don&#8217;t boil the gnocchi here. Instead, I bake it in the oven alongside cherry tomatoes. The gnocchi soaks up the flavorful tomato juices while becoming lightly crisp and browned. After baking, I finish it with torn mozzarella, basil, and dollops of pesto for bold, [&hellip;]<div style="clear:both"></div>]]></description>
		
