					<description><![CDATA[<img width="1740" height="2439" src="https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/zucchini-muffins-recipe.jpg" class="attachment-feed-image size-feed-image wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/zucchini-muffins-recipe.jpg 1740w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/zucchini-muffins-recipe-214x300.jpg 214w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/zucchini-muffins-recipe-731x1024.jpg 731w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/zucchini-muffins-recipe-71x100.jpg 71w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/zucchini-muffins-recipe-580x813.jpg 580w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/zucchini-muffins-recipe-1160x1626.jpg 1160w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1740px) 100vw, 1740px" /><br />This zucchini muffins recipe is one of my favorite ways to use up summer zucchini. A perfect breakfast or snack, the muffins are sweet, soft, and incredibly moist, thanks to 2 whole cups of shredded zucchini inside them. Vanilla, nutmeg, and cinnamon fill them with warm, spiced depth of flavor, and walnuts add delicious crunch. (If you&#8217;re wondering—yes, chocolate chips would work here too!) This zucchini muffins recipe is an updated version of one I shared back in 2021. I recently re-tested it and updated it to be more similar to my go-to zucchini bread recipe, using a streamlined ingredient list [&hellip;]<div style="clear:both"></div>]]></description>
		
